1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
CIRCULATOR: Patient is a 68-year-old for a right total knee replacement, primary osteoarthritis.

2
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:29,000
ANESTHESIA: Plan is spinal anesthesia with sedation. Spinal is in, good level, patient comfortable.

3
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:11,000
SURGEON: Time out. Right total knee arthroplasty, correct patient, site marked and confirmed, antibiotics given.

4
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
ANESTHESIA: Cefazolin 2 grams IV given 20 minutes ago.

5
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:36,000
SURGEON: Tourniquet up at 300 millimeters of mercury. Time is noted.

6
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:15,000
SURGEON: Midline skin incision, medial parapatellar approach.

7
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:08,000
SURGEON: Good exposure. Making the distal femoral cut now with the jig.

8
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:38,000
SURGEON: Trial components in. Knee is stable through range of motion, tracking well.

9
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:10,000
SURGEON: Cementing the final components. Femoral component, tibial baseplate, and patellar button.

10
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:28,000
SURGEON: Cement is cured. Final implants are in. All-polyethylene patella, cruciate-retaining design.

11
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:05,000
SURGEON: Releasing the tourniquet now. Total tourniquet time 29 minutes.

12
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:22,000
SURGEON: Hemostasis is good. Minimal bleeding. Estimated blood loss is about 50 mils.

13
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:06,000
SURGEON: Closing in layers. No drain needed.

14
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:37,000
CIRCULATOR: Sponge, sharp, and instrument counts are correct times two.

15
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:07,000
ANESTHESIA: Patient did well throughout. Hemodynamically stable the entire case, no pressors.

16
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:40,000
SURGEON: Dressing on. For handoff: routine primary TKA, uncomplicated, EBL 50, no drain, spinal still working.

17
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:09,000
ANESTHESIA: To PACU, then the orthopedic floor. Routine pathway, physical therapy can start today.

18
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:35,000
SURGEON: Weight bearing as tolerated. I'll speak with the family.
